  "causebase_summary": "International China Concern (Australia) Ltd is an ACNC‑registered entity with a web presence at chinaconcern.org and structured geography recorded as Victoria, Australia. Publicly available website text describes its privacy and website practices: it collects visitors’ IP addresses and linked data for server administration and aggregate analysis, uses cookies, transmits information via SSL encryption, and names third‑party payment/transaction providers (FundraiseUp, GiftTool, Raisely, Charities Aid Foundation, Mollie). The site includes a published Complaints Policy that references five elements (Culture, Principles, People, Process, Analysis), states the policy is modelled on biblical principles, and sets out a seven‑stage complaint process (acknowledgement, assessment, planning, investigation, response, review, consideration of systemic issues). The policy says complaints will ideally be acknowledged within two business days and that the organisation will report progress if a complaint is not finalised within seven days; it also permits anonymous complaints and use of external investigators. Regulatory financial reporting (ACNC AIS 2023) shows revenue of AUD 899,398 and total expenses of AUD 945,189 for the 2023 reporting year (organisation‑level reporting).",
